 # Span Space Isosurface Extraction
 
-Also called: Span Space Algorithm, Livat, Shen, and Johnson method
+Also called: ISSUE, Isosurface Extraction using Span Space, Livat, Shen, and Johnson method, Near Optimal Isosurface Extraction Algorithm using the Span Space, Span Space Algorithm
 
 ## Overview
-Span Space Isosurface Extraction is a method for rapidly locating all volume cells intersecting a specific isovalue by mapping cell scalar extrema into a 2D coordinate system known as "span space" [S1, book]. It solves the problem of efficient active cell identification in large datasets by reducing the search to a 2D range query, achieving a worst-case search complexity of $O(\sqrt{n} + k)$, where $n$ is the dataset size and $k$ is the number of cells in the isosurface [S1, book]. It differs from sibling methods by explicitly leveraging the geometric properties of min/max value pairs in a 2D plane rather than relying solely on hierarchical spatial subdivision of the domain [6891-span-space-decomposition.md].
+Span Space Isosurface Extraction rapidly locates all volume cells intersecting a specific isovalue by mapping cell scalar extrema into a 2D coordinate system known as "span space" [S2, book]. It solves the problem of efficient active cell identification in large datasets by reducing the search to a 2D range query, achieving a worst-case search complexity of $O(\sqrt{n} + k)$, where $n$ is the dataset size and $k$ is the number of cells in the isosurface [S2, book]. It differs from sibling methods by explicitly leveraging the geometric properties of min/max value pairs in a 2D plane rather than relying solely on hierarchical spatial subdivision of the domain [6891-span-space-decomposition.md][S3, unofficial].
 
